OK so I had an orcish ranger, got up to xp level 9 or so, and was
doing Sokoban. I was up to the final level (Bag of Holding), was
starting to move around some boulders to make room, and one of them
said "you hear a monster behind it, that's why you cannot move it".
Great. I'm pretty sure this thing really needs to be moved to complete
the level. There's another boulder blocking getting around the back of
the problem boulder, and if I move that it gets stuck into a corner,
which I have a feeling could ruin the chances of completing this
(especially as I don't have a pickaxe to smash boulders and take the
luck hit). So I take off and drop every single item I own, and try and
move onto the boulder. "There's a boulder here... you try and squeeze
past". Suddenly, the boulder turns into a giant mimic! Who starts
wailing on me. Try and run away? "You can't escape the giant mimic!".
I have no equipment whatsoever. He's got me at about 15 hp out of max
60 or so, so I don't think praying is going to help me. I try punching
him in the face and he kills me.

So was there anything I could have done here? I think my biggest
mistake was dropping my stuff a couple of squares away (don't ask me
why, total brain fart, I'm still a newbie). If I had dropped it where
I was, then tried to move onto the boulder, I guess he would have
turned into a mimic and I would still be on the square with all my
gear on the floor in front of me, so I could have picked up a scroll
of teleport etc... wait that wouldn't have helped, Sokoban is no
teleport. At least a potion of healing, wand of sleep, etc. I can't
see how I would have had time to wield weapons, put on armour, etc
before killed me.

Assuming I couldn't get to my gear, was there any way out of this, or
was it YAV,V,VSD?


